binbun's bundled themes
=======================

The themes in gui/app/themes/ are built into binbun's GUI. Each maps an
upstream theme's own colours onto binbun's roles: the interface from the
upstream's workbench (UI) colours, code from its token colours, and
binbun's own roles (mnemonics, registers, addresses, xref comments, link
tints, the lit area, agreed) chosen by hand from the theme's palette by
the rule written in each file's header. The colours are the upstream's;
the files are binbun's. Each file's header repeats its credit below and
says where a role had no upstream colour and what it took instead.

All are under the MIT licence except where said (Tokyo Night Day: also
Apache-2.0). Each repository's licence text, as it stands at the commit
named, is in third_party/themes/ (owner-repository.txt; Zed's is that of
assets/themes/one/); the app's downloads carry this file and those texts
in licenses/.


